#name;Hank
Good evening, contessa. How are you?

#name;Imelda
Oh, Henry, dear, you know how much I dislike you calling me that.

#name;Hank
And YOU know how much I dislike you calling me Henry.

#name;Imelda
Well, fine. (Both chuckle.) It’s been too long, darling. And to answer your question, I’m absolutely dreadful.

**[Trouble in paradise?] ->Paridise

==Paridise==
#name;Hank
Trouble in paradise?

#name;Imelda
You could say that.

#name;Hank
What’s the matter, doll?

#name;Imelda
...I found the other woman. Some poor, sweet twenty-something. When I heard, I nearly chucked my pocketbook out the window. 

**[Are we surprised?] ->Surprise

==Surprise==

#name;Hank
Are we surprised?

#name;Imelda
You’re right, of course. But it hurts, all the same... I had a life before the Don, you know.

#name;Hank
Do I ever! I remember when every club promoter in the city would saw a leg off to hear you sing.

#name;Imelda
And now... look at me! I’m washed up! He’s gotta pay. Hank? Will you do me a favor? (A beat. The grisly implication of her request hangs in the air.)

**[I don’t like where this is going.] ->Going


==Going==
#name;Hank
I don’t like where this is going.

#name;Imelda
It doesn’t matter. With the Tagliatelle land grab, he’ll be swimming with the fishes by St Patrick’s either way. I’ll just be expediting the process. Besides, you won’t be implicated.

#name;Hank
And how is that?

#name;Imelda
 Cassio.

**[Baloney.]->Baloney

                
==Baloney==

#name;Hank
Baloney.

#name;Imelda
He’s in love with me.

**[He’s more in love with his position.]

#name;Hank
He’s more in love with his position.

#name;Imelda
Well, my husband will leave a vacuum.

#name;Hank
And you think that slimeball can fill his shoes? 

#name;Imelda
That’s irrelevant. Trust me. 

#name;Hank
I do... but–

#name;Imelda
Trust. Me.

***[You’re gonna be the death of me]. ->Death
    

==Death==
#name;Hank
(sighs.) You’re gonna be the death of me.

The cab slows, turning onto a busy downtown street filled with neon lights and bustling silhouettes.

#name;Imelda
 Nonsense. You’re going to be the death of my husband. (She hands him a thick envelope.)

 The cab pulls up to SAMBUCA, the Pappardelle crime family’s downtown base.

#name;Hank
I pray you’re right. Now, split before I change my mind. And–(he kisses her hand) knock ‘em dead.

**knock ‘em dead.

#name;Imelda
You won’t regret this. (She exits the vehicle, slinks away, and disappears into SAMBUCA.)

-> END

